ollow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original evidence and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new sources or places."]},"subject":"Geography","success_criteria":["I can use reduce with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify reuse and explain why it matters.","I can practise recycle independently on a new prompt.","I can notice wisely needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Using resources wisely means using less, using things again and recycling materials so fewer new resources are taken. Reduce, reuse, recycle and repair all help. Saving water and energy at home and school also protects resources. Supported records follow the actual sources and…","options":["A guess with no evidence.","Using resources wisely means using less, using things again and recycling materials so fewer new resources are taken. Reduce, reuse, recycle and repair all help. Saving water and energy at home and school also protects resources.","A claim unrelated to the source or place.","An answer copied without understanding."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about reduce?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: a family fixes a dripping tap, takes a short shower and turns off lights in empty rooms. They use a jar as a pencil holder and put cans in the recycling bin. The class records which action reduces, reuses or recycles.\n\nTRY FIRST\nSort into reduce, reuse or recycle: buying fewer plastic wraps; using a jar as a pencil holder; putting cans in the recycling bin.\n\nFEEDBACK\nReduce: buying fewer plastic wraps. Reuse: the jar as a pencil holder. Recycle: cans in the recycling bin.","explain":"Using resources wisely means using less, using things again and recycling materials so fewer new resources are taken. Reduce, reuse, recycle and repair all help. Saving water and energy at home and school also protects 